data: {"level":2,"reviewed":{"level":2,"label":"formula / approach","text":"For each new value x, with count n after including it: delta = x − mean (using the old mean),\nmean ← mean + delta / n, and M2 ← M2 + delta · (x − mean) (using the new mean). At the end,\nthe sample variance is M2 / (n − 1). Raise `ValueError` before dividing when the count is zero."},"hints_note":null}

